@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# json-dive
+
+Explore and query JSON files with intuitive path navigation. A fast, zero-dependency CLI tool that makes working with JSON in the terminal a breeze.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Dot-notation paths**: Navigate with `users[0].name` instead of complex jq syntax
+- **Array filtering**: Filter arrays with simple conditions like `age>25` or `name~alice`
+- **Interactive REPL**: Explore JSON interactively with path navigation
+- **Syntax highlighting**: Color-coded output (strings=green, numbers=magenta, booleans=yellow)
+- **Type inspection**: View the type and length of any value
+- **Zero dependencies**: Pure Python, works anywhere Python 3.8+ runs
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+pip install json-dive
+```
+
+Or install from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-dive.git
+cd json-dive
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Basic Queries
+
+```bash
+# Pretty-print a JSON file
+json-dive data.json
+
+# Navigate to a specific path
+json-dive data.json -p "users[0].name"
+# => "Alice Martin"
+
+# Show keys at a path
+json-dive data.json -p "config" --keys
+# => debug (boolean): False
+#    max_connections (integer): 100
+#    features (object): {3 keys}
+#    api_keys (object): {2 keys}
+
+# Show array with indices
+json-dive data.json -p "users" --index
+# => [0] {id, name, email, age, roles, address}
+#    [1] {id, name, email, age, roles, address}
+#    [2] {id, name, email, age, roles, address}
+```
+
+### Array Filtering
+
+```bash
+# Filter users older than 30
+json-dive data.json -p "users" --filter "age>30"
+
+# Filter by string match
+json-dive data.json -p "users" --filter "name~alice"
+
+# Filter by equality
+json-dive data.json -p "users" --filter "id=2"
+```
+
+### Output Formats
+
+```bash
+# Raw JSON (no colors)
+json-dive data.json -p "users[0]" --raw
+
+# Compact output
+json-dive data.json --compact
+
+# Show type information
+json-dive data.json -p "users" --type
+# => Type: array
