+# curl-format
+
+Format, colorize, and convert curl commands. Makes complex curl commands readable at a glance.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Syntax highlighting** — method, URL, headers, and body each in distinct colors
+- **Pretty print** — multi-line format with one flag per line
+- **Compact mode** — squeeze into a single clean line
+- **HTTPie conversion** — convert curl commands to HTTPie syntax
+- **Pipe-friendly** — read from stdin or pass as arguments
+- **Smart parsing** — handles quoted strings, line continuations, and all common curl flags
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/curl-format@latest
+
+# Or clone and build
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/curl-format.git
+cd curl-format
+make build
+sudo make install
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Pretty print a curl command
+echo 'curl -X POST https://api.example.com/users -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"name\":\"Alice\"}"' | curl-format --pretty -s
+
+# Colored output (default)
+curl-format 'curl https://api.example.com'
+
+# Convert to HTTPie
+echo 'curl -X POST https://api.example.com -H "X-Custom: val" -d "data"' | curl-format --httpie -s
+
+# Pipe from clipboard (macOS)
+pbpaste | curl-format --pretty -s
+
+# Pipe from clipboard (Linux)
+xclip -o | curl-format --pretty -s
+```
+
+## Examples
+
+### Input
+```
+curl -X POST https://api.example.com/users -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "Authorization: Bearer token" -d '{"name":"Alice","age":30}'
+```
+
+### Pretty output
+```
+curl -X POST \
+  https://api.example.com/users \
+  -H 'Content-Type:application/json' \
+  -H 'Authorization:Bearer token' \
+  -d '{"name":"Alice","age":30}'
+```
+
+### HTTPie output
+```
+http post https://api.example.com/users Authorization:'Bearer token' {"name":"Alice","age":30}
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Short | Description |
+|------|-------|-------------|
+| `--pretty` | `-p` | Multi-line format |
+| `--compact` | `-c` | Single-line format |
+| `--httpie` | | Convert to HTTPie |
+| `--stdin` | `-s` | Read from stdin |
+| `--no-color` | `-n` | Disable colors |
+
+## Supported curl flags
+
+`-X`, `-H`, `-d`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `-u`, `-b`, `-L`, `-k`, `--compressed`, `-v`
