+# port-scanner
+
+A fast, concurrent TCP port scanner written in Go. Scan single hosts with configurable concurrency, timeouts, and output formats.
+
+## Features
+
+- Concurrent scanning with configurable workers (default: 100)
+- Port presets (common, web, database, mail)
+- Custom port ranges (e.g. `80,443,8000-9000`)
+- JSON output for scripting and piping
+- Service name detection for well-known ports
+- Latency measurement per port
+- Verbose mode to show closed ports
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# Install with Go
+go install github.com/TataneSan/port-scanner/cmd@latest
+
+# Or build from source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/port-scanner.git
+cd port-scanner
+go build -o port-scanner ./cmd
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Scan common ports (default)
+port-scanner example.com
+
+# Scan specific ports
+port-scanner -p 22,80,443 192.168.1.1
+
+# Scan a port range with high concurrency
+port-scanner -p 1-1024 -w 500 example.com
+
+# Use a preset
+port-scanner -preset web example.com
+port-scanner -preset database 10.0.0.5
+
+# JSON output for scripting
+port-scanner -json -p 22,80,443 example.com
+
+# Verbose: show closed ports too
+port-scanner -v -p 1-100 localhost
+
+# Custom timeout
+port-scanner -t 500ms -p 1-1000 example.com
+```
+
+## Port Presets
+
+| Preset     | Ports                                                    |
+|------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
+| `common`   | Top 30 most common ports (default when no -p specified)  |
+| `web`      | HTTP/HTTPS ports: 80, 443, 3000, 5000, 8000, 8080, ...  |
+| `database` | MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, Oracle, MSSQL, ...    |
+| `mail`     | SMTP, POP3, IMAP and their TLS variants                 |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Scan a web server
+```
+$ port-scanner -preset web example.com
+
+Scanning example.com (93.184.216.34) ...
+
+  example.com:80     open    http             12ms
+  example.com:443    open    https            15ms
+
+--- Scan complete ---
+Host:     example.com
+Scanned:  9 ports
+Open:     2
+Closed:   7
+Duration: 1.02s
