+# env-check
+
+Check for missing environment variables in your project. Reads `.env.example` (or similar) and compares against your current environment.
+
+## Features
+
+- Auto-detects `.env.example`, `.env.sample`, `.env.template`
+- Shows missing, empty, and set variables with color-coded output
+- JSON output for CI/CD pipelines
+- Generate `.env` templates from example files
+- Strict mode for CI (exits non-zero on missing vars)
+- Supports commented-out optional variables
+- Descriptions from inline comments
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+pip install git+https://github.com/TataneSan/env-check.git
+
+# Or from source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-check.git
+cd env-check
+pip install -e .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Auto-detect .env.example in current directory
+env-check
+
+# Check against a specific file
+env-check -f .env.sample
+
+# Show all variables (including set ones)
+env-check --all
+
+# JSON output for CI
+env-check --json
+
+# Generate .env template
+env-check --generate > .env
+
+# Strict mode: exit 1 if any vars missing (for CI)
+env-check --strict
+```
+
+## .env.example Format
+
+```bash
+# Database connection
+DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/mydb
+
+# API keys (required, no default)
+API_KEY=
+SECRET_KEY=
+
+# Optional: Redis (commented out = optional)
+# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
+
+# With default value
+PORT=3000
+LOG_LEVEL=info
+```
+
+**Rules:**
+- `VAR=` — required, no default (will show as MISSING if not set)
+- `VAR=default` — required, uses default if not in environment
+- `# VAR` or `# VAR=default` — optional (commented out)
+- `# description` — attached as description to the next variable
+
+## Examples
+
+### All vars set
+```
+  ✓ All environment variables are set!
+```
+
