+# log-tail
+
+Tail log files with automatic color-coding by log level. Supports follow mode, level filtering, grep patterns, and works with stdin.
+
+## Features
+
+- Auto-detects log levels: FATAL, ERROR, WARN, INFO, DEBUG, TRACE
+- Color-coded output (red for errors, yellow for warnings, green for info, cyan for debug)
+- Follow mode (`-f`) for live tailing like `tail -f`
+- Filter by minimum log level
+- Grep pattern matching
+- Works with stdin (pipe-friendly)
+- Level statistics summary
+- Supports common log formats (log4j, Python logging, syslog, nginx, etc.)
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+pip install git+https://github.com/TataneSan/log-tail.git
+
+# Or from source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/log-tail.git
+cd log-tail
+pip install -e .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Colorized tail of last 20 lines
+log-tail app.log
+
+# Follow mode (live tailing)
+log-tail -f app.log
+
+# Show last 100 lines
+log-tail -n 100 app.log
+
+# Only show WARN and above
+log-tail -l warn app.log
+
+# Only show ERROR and above
+log-tail -l error app.log
+
+# Grep for specific pattern
+log-tail -g 'timeout|connection' app.log
+
+# Pipe from another command
+docker logs mycontainer | log-tail
+
+# Show statistics at the end
+log-tail --stats app.log
+
+# No colors (for piping to file)
+log-tail --no-color app.log
+```
+
+## Log Level Colors
+
+| Level    | Color          | Detected keywords                        |
+|----------|----------------|------------------------------------------|
+| FATAL    | Bold Red       | FATAL, CRITICAL, EMERG, PANIC            |
+| ERROR    | Red            | ERROR, ERR, SEVERE                       |
+| WARN     | Yellow         | WARN, WARNING                            |
+| INFO     | Green          | INFO, NOTICE                             |
+| DEBUG    | Cyan           | DEBUG, DBG                               |
+| TRACE    | Dim White      | TRACE, TRC, FINE, FINEST                 |
+
+## Supported Log Formats
+
+Works with any log format that contains level keywords:
+
+```
+# Python logging
+2026-01-15 10:30:45 ERROR app.module: Something failed
+
+# Java/Log4j
+2026-01-15 10:30:45.123 [main] ERROR com.app.Service - Connection failed
