+# file-watcher
+
+> Watch files and run commands on change — a fast, minimal alternative to nodemon.
+
+A lightweight CLI tool that monitors your files and automatically re-runs a command when changes are detected. Perfect for development workflows where you want instant feedback.
+
+## Features
+
+- ⚡ **Fast** — uses chokidar for efficient filesystem watching
+- 🎯 **Smart filtering** — watch by file extension
+- ⏱️ **Debounced** — avoids rapid re-runs during bulk saves
+- 🧹 **Clean output** — timestamps, colored prefixes, optional terminal clearing
+- 🔄 **Auto-restart** — optionally restart when the process exits
+- 💀 **Signal control** — choose how to kill the previous process
+- 🪶 **Minimal** — zero config, just point and run
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Global
+npm install -g file-watcher
+
+# Or use npx
+npx file-watcher "node server.js"
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+file-watcher <command> [options]
+```
+
+The binary is also aliased as `fw` for shorter typing:
+
+```bash
+fw "python app.py"
+```
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-w, --watch <paths...>` | Paths to watch | `.` |
+| `-e, --ext <extensions>` | File extensions (comma-separated) | `js,ts,json,yaml,yml,toml,py,go,rs,html,css,scss` |
+| `-i, --ignore <patterns...>` | Patterns to ignore | `node_modules, .git, dist, build` |
+| `-d, --delay <ms>` | Debounce delay in ms | `300` |
+| `-c, --clear` | Clear terminal before re-run | `false` |
+| `-r, --restart-on-exit` | Restart even if process exits cleanly | `false` |
+| `-s, --signal <signal>` | Signal to kill previous process | `SIGTERM` |
+| `--no-colors` | Disable colored output | — |
+| `-V, --version` | Show version | — |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help | — |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Watch and restart a Node.js server
+
+```bash
+file-watcher "node server.js"
+```
+
+### Watch only Python files
+
+```bash
+file-watcher "python app.py" -e py
+```
+
+### Watch specific directories with terminal clearing
+
+```bash
+file-watcher "go run ." -w ./cmd ./internal -e go -c
+```
+
+### Watch with auto-restart on exit (for flaky scripts)
+
+```bash
+file-watcher "npm test" -r
+```
