+# hash-gen
+
+> Generate hashes with multiple algorithms — md5, sha256, blake2, sha3, and more.
+
+A fast CLI tool for computing hashes from strings, files, or stdin. Supports 12 algorithms including HMAC computation.
+
+## Features
+
+- 🔐 **12 algorithms** — md5, sha1, sha2 family, sha3 family, blake2
+- 📁 **File hashing** — hash any file with `-f`
+- 🔧 **HMAC support** — compute HMAC with a secret key
+- 📥 **Stdin support** — pipe data directly
+- 🔤 **Case control** — uppercase or lowercase hex output
+- 🎯 **All-at-once** — hash with every algorithm simultaneously
+- ⚡ **Zero dependencies beyond Node.js stdlib** — commander + picocolors only
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Global
+npm install -g hash-gen
+
+# Or use npx
+npx hash-gen "hello world"
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+hash-gen [input] [options]
+```
+
+Short alias: `hg`
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-a, --algo <algorithm>` | Hash algorithm | `sha256` |
+| `-A, --all` | Hash with all algorithms | `false` |
+| `-f, --file <path>` | Hash a file | — |
+| `-H, --hmac <key>` | Compute HMAC with key | — |
+| `-u, --uppercase` | Output uppercase hex | `false` |
+| `-l, --list` | List available algorithms | — |
+| `-q, --quiet` | Output only the hash | `false` |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Hash a string
+
+```bash
+hash-gen "hello world"
+# sha256  b94d27b9934d3e08a52e52d7da7dabfac484efe37a5380ee9088f7ace2efcde9
+```
+
+### Use a specific algorithm
+
+```bash
+hash-gen "hello world" -a md5
+# md5  5eb63bbbe01eeed093cb22bb8f5acdc3
+```
+
+### Hash with all algorithms
+
+```bash
+hash-gen "hello" -A
+# md5        5d41402abc4b2a76b9719d911017c592
+# sha1       aaf4c61ddcc5e8a2dabede0f3b482cd9aea9434d
+# sha256     2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824
+# ...
+```
+
+### Hash a file
+
+```bash
+hash-gen -f /path/to/file
+hash-gen -f package.json -a sha256
+hash-gen -f image.png -A
