+# qr-gen
+
+> Generate QR codes in terminal (ASCII) or as PNG/SVG images.
+
+A fast CLI tool for creating QR codes. Display them directly in your terminal or save them as image files.
+
+## Features
+
+- 🖥️ **Terminal display** — colored block characters that scan with your phone
+- 🖼️ **Image export** — PNG and SVG output
+- 📁 **File input** — encode file contents
+- 📥 **Stdin support** — pipe data from other commands
+- 🎨 **Customizable** — colors, margins, dark mode
+- ℹ️ **Info mode** — inspect QR code metadata
+- ⚡ **Fast** — instant generation
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Global
+npm install -g qr-gen
+
+# Or use npx
+npx qr-gen "https://github.com"
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+qr-gen <data> [options]
+```
+
+Short alias: `qr`
+
+## Examples
+
+### Display in terminal
+
+```bash
+qr-gen "https://github.com"
+qr "Hello, World!"
+```
+
+### Save as PNG
+
+```bash
+qr-gen "https://github.com" -o qrcode.png
+qr-gen "https://github.com" -o qr.png -W 500
+```
+
+### Save as SVG
+
+```bash
+qr-gen "https://github.com" -o qrcode.svg
+```
+
+### Dark terminal mode
+
+```bash
+qr-gen "https://github.com" --invert
+```
+
+### Encode file contents
+
+```bash
+qr-gen -f secret.txt -o secret-qr.png
+```
+
+### Pipe from stdin
+
+```bash
+echo "https://github.com" | qr-gen
+cat url.txt | qr-gen -o link.png
+```
+
+### Custom colors
+
+```bash
