+# screenshot-api
+
+> REST API for capturing screenshots of web pages.
+
+A self-hosted API that uses Puppeteer to take screenshots, generate PDFs, and capture specific elements from any URL. Perfect for automated testing, preview generation, or archiving.
+
+## Features
+
+- 📸 **Screenshot capture** — PNG or JPEG output
+- 📄 **PDF generation** — full page PDFs
+- 🎯 **Element capture** — screenshot specific CSS selectors
+- 📐 **Custom viewport** — any resolution
+- 🔄 **Full page** — capture entire scrollable page
+- ⏱️ **Configurable** — timeout, wait strategy, delay
+- 🛡️ **Secure** — rate limiting, CORS, Helmet headers
+- 🐳 **Docker ready** — included Dockerfile
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Install
+npm install
+
+# Start server
+npm start
+# → http://localhost:3000
+```
+
+## Docker
+
+```bash
+docker build -t screenshot-api .
+docker run -p 3000:3000 screenshot-api
+```
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### `POST /api/screenshot`
+
+Capture a screenshot with JSON body.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"url": "https://github.com"}' \
+  -o screenshot.png
+```
+
+### `GET /api/screenshot`
+
+Capture with query parameters.
+
+```bash
+# Basic
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot?url=https://github.com" -o shot.png
+
+# Custom size + JPEG
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot?url=https://github.com&width=1920&height=1080&format=jpeg&quality=90" -o shot.jpg
+
+# Full page
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot?url=https://github.com&fullPage=true" -o full.png
+
+# Specific element
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot?url=https://github.com&selector=.Header" -o header.png
+
+# With delay (for JS-heavy pages)
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/screenshot?url=https://example.com&delay=2000" -o shot.png
+```
+
+### `GET /api/pdf`
+
+Generate a PDF of a web page.
+
+```bash
+curl "http://localhost:3000/api/pdf?url=https://github.com" -o page.pdf
+```
+
+### `GET /health`
