+# image-compress-api
+
+Compress JPEG, PNG, and WEBP images via a simple REST API. No LLM, no external services — just pure Pillow image processing.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Multi-format**: JPEG, PNG, WEBP input and output
+- **Format conversion**: Convert between supported formats
+- **Resize**: Optionally constrain max width/height
+- **Metadata stripping**: Remove EXIF data to save extra bytes
+- **Quality control**: 1-100 quality slider
+- **Stats endpoint**: Get compression stats without downloading the file
+- **Docker-ready**: Single command to deploy
+
+## Install
+
+### Local
+
+```bash
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker build -t image-compress-api .
+docker run -p 8000:8000 image-compress-api
+```
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### `GET /`
+
+Service info and available endpoints.
+
+### `GET /health`
+
+Health check.
+
+### `POST /compress`
+
+Upload an image and get the compressed version back.
+
+**Parameters** (multipart form):
+
+| Field | Type | Default | Description |
+|-------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `file` | file | required | Image file to compress |
+| `quality` | int | 80 | Compression quality 1-100 |
+| `format` | string | auto | Target format: jpeg, png, webp |
+| `max_width` | int | none | Max width in pixels |
+| `max_height` | int | none | Max height in pixels |
+| `strip_metadata` | bool | true | Remove EXIF metadata |
+
+**Response**: Compressed image file with headers:
+- `X-Original-Size`: Original file size in bytes
+- `X-Compressed-Size`: Compressed file size in bytes
+- `X-Savings-Percent`: Percentage reduction
+
+### `POST /compress/info`
+
+Same parameters as `/compress`, but returns JSON stats instead of the file.
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Compress with curl
+
+```bash
+# Basic compression
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/compress \
+  -F "file=@photo.jpg" \
+  -F "quality=70" \
+  -o compressed.jpg
+
+# Convert JPEG to WEBP
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/compress \
+  -F "file=@photo.jpg" \
