+# color-palette
+
+Extract color palettes from any URL — beautiful terminal display with ANSI colors.
+
+Fetches a web page, parses all CSS (inline styles, `<style>` tags, external stylesheets), extracts hex/rgb/hsl/named colors, deduplicates similar shades, and displays a beautiful palette right in your terminal.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Full CSS parsing** — hex, rgb(), rgba(), hsl(), hsla(), named colors
+- **External stylesheet fetching** — follows `<link rel="stylesheet">` tags
+- **Image color extraction** — dominant colors from favicon and og:image
+- **Smart deduplication** — merges visually similar colors (configurable threshold)
+- **Frequency ranking** — most-used colors appear first
+- **Multiple output formats** — terminal ANSI, JSON, CSS vars, SCSS, Tailwind
+- **Zero config** — just pass a URL and go
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+pip install .
+```
+
+Or directly:
+
+```bash
+pip install git+https://github.com/TataneSan/color-palette.git
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Basic — extract palette from any site
+color-palette https://github.com
+
+# JSON output
+color-palette https://stripe.com -f json
+
+# CSS custom properties
+color-palette https://tailwindcss.com -f css
+
+# SCSS variables
+color-palette https://vercel.com -f scss
+
+# Tailwind config
+color-palette https://linear.app -f tailwind
+
+# Skip image extraction, limit to 10 colors
+color-palette https://example.com --no-images -n 10
+
+# Adjust deduplication threshold (lower = more colors kept)
+color-palette https://dribbble.com --threshold 10
+```
+
+## Output Formats
+
+### Terminal (default)
+
+```
+🎨 Color Palette
+   Source: https://github.com
+   Page:   GitHub · Build and ship software
+   Found:  147 colors → 12 unique
+
+   ████████████  #0d1117     rgb(13, 17, 23)         42  hex
+   ████████████  #f0f6fc     rgb(240, 246, 252)      28  hex
+   ████████████  #58a6ff     rgb(88, 166, 255)       15  hex
+   ...
+```
+
+### JSON
+
+```json
+{
+  "url": "https://github.com",
+  "title": "GitHub · Build and ship software",
+  "colors": [
+    {"hex": "#0d1117", "rgb": [13, 17, 23], "count": 42, "source": "hex"}
+  ]
