-# ⏰ cron-parser
+# cron-parser
 
-Parse et explique les expressions cron en français. Affiche les prochaines exécutions et valide les expressions.
+Parse, explain, and preview cron expressions — right from your terminal.
 
-## Installation
+No dependencies. Pure Python. Just works.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Parse** any standard cron expression (5 or 6 fields)
+- **Explain** what a cron expression does in plain English
+- **Preview** the next N execution times
+- **Validate** expressions with clear error messages
+- **Browse** common cron expressions with `--list`
+- Supports ranges (`1-5`), steps (`*/15`), lists (`1,3,5`), and named values (`Mon`, `Jan`)
+- Reads from stdin or argument
+
+## Install
 
 ```bash
-pip install git+https://github.com/TataneSan/cron-parser.git
+# From PyPI
+pip install cron-parser-cli
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cron-parser.git
+cd cron-parser
+pip install .
 ```
 
-Ou en local :
-
-```bash
-git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cron-parser.git
-cd cron-parser
-pip install -e .
-```
+No external dependencies — uses only Python stdlib.
 
 ## Usage
 
+### Quick parse (default)
+
 ```bash
-# Analyser une expression cron
-cron-parser "*/5 * * * *"
-cron-parser "0 9 * * 1-5"
-cron-parser "@daily"
+$ cron-parser "*/5 * * * *"
 
-# Afficher les prochaines exécutions
-cron-parser --next 10 "0 */2 * * *"
+Expression: */5 * * * *
+  */5 (minute) | * (hour) | * (day of month) | * (month) | * (day of week)
+  → Runs every 5 minutes
 
