+# cert-check
+
+Check SSL certificate expiration for domains — right from your terminal.
+
+No dependencies. Pure Python. Just works.
+
+## Features
+
+- Check SSL certificates for multiple domains at once
+- Read domains from a file
+- Configurable warning/critical thresholds (default: 30d/7d)
+- Show certificate details: issuer, subject, SANs, cipher, protocol
+- Color-coded terminal output
+- JSON output for scripting
+- Nagios-compatible exit codes (0=ok, 1=warning, 2=critical)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# From PyPI
+pip install cert-check-cli
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cert-check.git
+cd cert-check
+pip install .
+```
+
+No external dependencies — uses only Python stdlib.
+
+## Usage
+
+### Check a single domain
+
+```bash
+$ cert-check example.com
+
+  Target                                        Status               Expires      Issuer
+  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+  example.com                                   ✔ 72d               2026-08-01   Let's Encrypt
+
+  Total: 1 | OK: 1 | Warning: 0 | Critical: 0
+```
+
+### Check multiple domains
+
+```bash
+$ cert-check google.com github.com cloudflare.com
+
+  Target                                        Status               Expires      Issuer
+  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+  google.com                                    ✔ 58d               2026-07-18   Google Trust Services
+  github.com                                    ✔ 365d              2027-05-20   DigiCert
+  cloudflare.com                                ✔ 245d              2027-01-21   Cloudflare
+
+  Total: 3 | OK: 3 | Warning: 0 | Critical: 0
+```
+
+### Check with custom port
+
+```bash
+$ cert-check myapp.example.com:8443
+```
+
+### Read domains from file
+
+```bash
+$ cat domains.txt
+example.com
+api.example.com
+app.example.com:8443
+
+$ cert-check -f domains.txt
+```
+
+### Custom thresholds
+
+```bash
