+# 🍅 pomodoro-cli
+
+A terminal Pomodoro timer with visual progress bar, session tracking in SQLite, and customizable durations.
+
+## Features
+
+- Visual countdown timer with progress bar
+- Automatic work/break cycle management
+- Long break every 4 rounds (configurable)
+- Session history stored in SQLite
+- Statistics by time period
+- Sound notification on completion
+- Graceful Ctrl+C interruption
+- Zero dependencies (Python stdlib only)
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# From PyPI
+pip install pomodoro-cli
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/pomodoro-cli.git
+cd pomodoro-cli
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Default session: 25min work, 5min break, 4 rounds
+pomodoro
+
+# Custom durations
+pomodoro -w 15 -s 3         # 15min work, 3min break
+pomodoro -w 50 -l 20 -r 6  # 50min work, 20min long break, 6 rounds
+
+# View statistics
+pomodoro stats              # Last 7 days
+pomodoro stats --days 30    # Last 30 days
+
+# Reset history
+pomodoro reset
+```
+
+## Options
+
+```
+-w, --work          Work duration in minutes (default: 25)
+-s, --short-break   Short break duration in minutes (default: 5)
+-l, --long-break    Long break duration in minutes (default: 15)
+-r, --rounds        Number of rounds (default: 4)
+```
+
+## Session Storage
+
+Sessions are stored in `~/.pomodoro/sessions.db` (SQLite). Override with:
+
+```bash
+export POMODORO_DB=/path/to/custom.db
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
