+# 📋 todo-cli
+
+A terminal task manager with SQLite persistence, priorities, tags, due dates, and markdown export.
+
+## Features
+
+- Add, edit, complete, and delete tasks
+- Three priority levels: high 🔴, medium 🟡, low 🔵
+- Tags for organization
+- Due dates with overdue detection
+- Filter by status, priority, or tag
+- Export to markdown
+- Statistics dashboard
+- Color-coded terminal output
+- Data stored locally in SQLite
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# From PyPI
+pip install todo-cli
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/todo-cli.git
+cd todo-cli
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Add tasks
+
+```bash
+todo add "Buy groceries"
+todo add "Deploy v2" -p high -t dev,urgent -d 2026-06-01
+todo add "Read docs" -p low -t learning
+```
+
+### List tasks
+
+```bash
+todo list                    # All tasks
+todo list --filter todo      # Only pending
+todo list --filter done      # Only completed
+todo list --tag dev          # Filter by tag
+todo list --priority high    # Filter by priority
+```
+
+### Manage tasks
+
+```bash
+todo done 3                  # Mark as completed
+todo undone 3                # Mark as pending again
+todo rm 5                    # Delete task
+todo edit 2 "New title" -p high -d 2026-07-01
+```
+
+### Stats and export
+
+```bash
+todo stats                   # Show statistics
+todo export                  # Print as markdown
+todo export -o tasks.md      # Save to file
+```
+
+## Data Storage
+
+Tasks are stored in `~/.todo/tasks.db` (SQLite). Override with:
+
+```bash
+export TODO_DB=/path/to/custom.db
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
