+# 🔐 password-gen
+
+A secure password generator for the terminal with multiple generation modes and strength analysis.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Random mode**: Configurable character sets (upper, lower, digits, symbols)
+- **Passphrase mode**: Word-based passwords (Diceware-style)
+- **Pronounceable mode**: Easy-to-read syllable-based passwords
+- Entropy calculation and strength meter
+- Exclude ambiguous characters (0/O, 1/l/I)
+- Generate multiple passwords at once
+- Password strength checker
+- Uses `secrets` module for cryptographic randomness
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# From PyPI
+pip install password-gen
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/password-gen.git
+cd password-gen
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Generate passwords
+
+```bash
+passgen                              # 20-char random password
+passgen -l 32 -u -d -s              # 32 chars with upper, digits, symbols
+passgen -n 5                         # Generate 5 passwords
+passgen --no-ambiguous               # Exclude ambiguous characters
+```
+
+### Passphrase mode
+
+```bash
+passgen --mode passphrase            # 4-word passphrase
+passgen --mode passphrase -w 6       # 6-word passphrase
+passgen --mode passphrase --capitalize --separator "."
+```
+
+### Pronounceable mode
+
+```bash
+passgen --mode pronounceable          # Easy to say password
+passgen --mode pronounceable -l 12    # 12-char pronounceable
+```
+
+### Check password strength
+
+```bash
+passgen check "my-password"
+```
+
+## Password Strength Levels
+
+| Entropy   | Level        | Description |
+|-----------|--------------|-------------|
+| < 28 bits | 🔴 Very Weak | Crackable in seconds |
+| < 36 bits | 🔴 Weak      | Crackable in minutes |
+| < 60 bits | 🟡 Medium    | Crackable in hours |
+| < 80 bits | 🟢 Strong    | Crackable in years |
+| ≥ 80 bits | 🟢 Very Strong | Practically unbreakable |
+
+## Security
+
+- Uses Python's `secrets` module (CSPRNG)
+- No passwords are stored or logged
+- Entropy calculations are accurate
+
+## License
+
+MIT
