+# 📝 notebook-cli
+
+A quick note-taking tool for the terminal with full-text search (FTS5), tags, and markdown export.
+
+## Features
+
+- Quick note capture from the terminal
+- Full-text search using SQLite FTS5
+- Tag-based organization
+- View, edit, and delete notes
+- Export to markdown
+- Pipe content from stdin
+- Color-coded terminal output
+- Data stored locally in SQLite
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# From PyPI
+pip install notebook-cli
+
+# From source
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/notebook-cli.git
+cd notebook-cli
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Add notes
+
+```bash
+notebook add "Project idea" -c "Build a CLI tool for X" -t idea,project
+notebook add "Meeting notes" -t work
+echo "Quick capture" | notebook add "Quick note"
+```
+
+### List notes
+
+```bash
+notebook list                    # All notes
+notebook list --tag work         # By tag
+notebook list --today            # Today's notes
+notebook list -n 5               # Last 5 notes
+```
+
+### View notes
+
+```bash
+notebook show 3                  # Full note content
+```
+
+### Search
+
+```bash
+notebook search "project"        # Full-text search
+notebook search "meeting" -n 5   # Limit results
+```
+
+### Edit and delete
+
+```bash
+notebook edit 3 "New title" -c "Updated content" -t updated
+notebook rm 5
+```
+
+### Tags and export
+
+```bash
+notebook tags                    # List all tags
+notebook export                  # Print as markdown
+notebook export -o notes.md      # Save to file
+```
+
+## Data Storage
+
+Notes are stored in `~/.notebook/notes.db` (SQLite with FTS5). Override with:
+
